//! How a program reaches an RP2350 (`b.flash(program, rp2350.flash.uf2)`): a file of blocks for
//! the chip's secure Arm cores, written by `picotool`, which finds the device on the bus whether or
//! not its drive is mounted, and, with `-f`, asks a running program with a USB console
//! (`rp2350.usb`) to reboot into BOOTSEL first, so the button is for a board that was never
//! flashed; else copied to the drive the boot ROM shows.

uf2: std.build.Flash = .uf2(.{
    .family = 0xe48b_ff59,
    .deliver = &[
        .run(.{ .command = "picotool", .args = &[.text("load"), .text("-f"), .text("-x"), .file] }),
        .drive(.{ .mark = "INFO_UF2.TXT" }),
    ],
});
